2700],[11.81,11.84,11.6,11.77,644600],[11.83,11.92,11.49,11.51,867600],[11.6,11.72,11.37,11.39,645000]],"about":{"what":"Halozyme Therapeutics, Inc. (HALO). This chart runs from Oct 21, 2011 to Mar 1, 2012.","setup":"The stock rose about 75% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 4 weeks, peaking at $9.80 and pulling back 9% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Jan 11, 2012 it closed at $9.97, its first close above the base high of $9.80. Volume that day was 1.3M shares, 3.60x the prior 10-day average of 358K. It held, never closing below the level three days running, reached a best close of $11.77, and the chart ends at $11.39.","lesson":"This is an example of a textbook breakout: a base, then a close above it on heavy volume, and it held. This is the pattern the rules are built around."}}